## 🎬 Part 1 — Screen Recording / Streaming Setup

### Option A: Local Recording Only (OBS Studio)
1. Download **OBS Studio** → [obsproject.com](https://obsproject.com) (free, open-source)
2. Open OBS → **Auto-Configuration Wizard** → choose **"Optimize for recording"**
3. **Sources** panel → `+` → **Display Capture** → select your monitor
4. (Optional) `+` → **Audio Input Capture** → select your mic
5. **Settings → Output → Recording Path** → choose a folder
6. Set recording format to **MKV** (safest for crashes) or **MP4**
7. Hit **Start Recording** before you open VS Code

### Option B: Stream to YouTube / Twitch
1. Same OBS setup, but in **Auto-Config Wizard** choose **"Optimize for streaming"**
2. **Settings → Stream → Service** → pick Twitch or YouTube
3. Paste your **Stream Key** (get it from your Twitch/YouTube dashboard)
4. Hit **Start Streaming**

### VS Code Layout for Stream
- Font size ≥ 16 (Ctrl+`,` → `editor.fontSize`)
- Theme: **One Dark Pro** or **GitHub Dark** (readable on stream)
- Open **both** files you'll edit side by side:
  - `Program.cs` on the left
  - [Controllers/HomeController.cs](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Desktop/Coded/intisor/MalfuzatExplorer/Controllers/HomeController.cs) on the right
- Open the **Terminal** panel (it shows your live builds — looks great on stream)

