### STEP 1 — Register `IMemoryCache` in `Program.cs`
**File:** `Program.cs`  
**Time estimate:** ~2 min

Open `Program.cs`. It currently looks like this:
```csharp
var builder = WebApplication.CreateBuilder(args);
builder.Services.AddControllersWithViews();
var app = builder.Build();
```

Position your cursor on the blank line **after** `AddControllersWithViews();` and type this comment:

```
// In-process result cache: stores up to 500 search result entries
```

**Copilot will suggest:**
```csharp
builder.Services.AddMemoryCache(options =>
{
    options.SizeLimit = 500;
});
```

✅ Accept it. Done.

**Say on stream:**
> *"This registers the IMemoryCache service with a hard cap of 500 entries — so the cache can never blow up our memory even if someone searches 500 different queries."*

---

### STEP 2 — Add `using` + Static Fields to `HomeController.cs`
**File:** [Controllers/HomeController.cs](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Desktop/Coded/intisor/MalfuzatExplorer/Controllers/HomeController.cs)  
**Time estimate:** ~5 min

**2a. Add the missing `using`**

At the top of the file, after the existing `using` statements, add:
```csharp
using Microsoft.Extensions.Caching.Memory;
```

**2b. Replace the instance `pdfFiles` field with static versions**

Find the current field declaration:
```csharp
private string[] pdfFiles = new string[]
{
    Path.Combine(Directory.GetCurrentDirectory(), "wwwroot", "Malfuzat", "Malfuzat-1.pdf"),
    // ... etc
};
```

**Delete it entirely.** Replace with:
```csharp
// ── static: path list is resolved once at startup, not per-request ──
private static readonly string[] _pdfFiles = new[]
{
    "Malfuzat-1.pdf", "Malfuzat-2.pdf", "Malfuzat-3.pdf",
    "Malfuzat-4.pdf", "Malfuzat-7.pdf", "Malfuzat-8.pdf",
    "Malfuzat-9.pdf", "Malfuzat-10.pdf"
};

private static readonly Regex _arabicRegex =
    new(@"[\u0600-\u06FF\u0750-\u077F\uFB50-\uFDFF\uFE70-\uFEFF]+",
        RegexOptions.Compiled);
```

**Copilot prompt to type** (as a comment above the Regex line):
```
// compiled once, reused across all requests
```
Copilot will fill in the `new Regex(...)` line for you.

**Say on stream:**
> *"Two things here. First — the file names only, not full paths. We'll resolve the full path via IWebHostEnvironment in the constructor. Second — this Arabic regex was being recompiled from scratch on every search result. With `RegexOptions.Compiled` and `static readonly`, it's JIT-compiled to native code once and never touched again."*

