### STEP 3 — Inject Dependencies (Constructor)
**File:** [Controllers/HomeController.cs](file:///c:/Users/DELL/Desktop/Coded/intisor/MalfuzatExplorer/Controllers/HomeController.cs)  
**Time estimate:** ~5 min

The current controller has **no constructor**. Add one right after the static fields:

```csharp
private readonly IMemoryCache _cache;
private readonly ILogger<HomeController> _logger;
private readonly IWebHostEnvironment _env;

public HomeController(IMemoryCache cache, ILogger<HomeController> logger, IWebHostEnvironment env)
{
    _cache = cache;
    _logger = logger;
    _env = env;
}

// Returns the full path for a given volume filename
private string PdfPath(string fileName) =>
    Path.Combine(_env.WebRootPath, "Malfuzat", fileName);
```

**Copilot prompt:** Type `public HomeController(` and Copilot will suggest all three parameters. Accept. Then type `// Returns the full path` and it will suggest the `PdfPath` helper.

**Say on stream:**
> *"Now the controller is fully testable. We can mock IMemoryCache, ILogger, and IWebHostEnvironment in unit tests. And `PdfPath` replaces the old `Directory.GetCurrentDirectory()` hack — WebRootPath is the correct, environment-aware way to resolve wwwroot paths in ASP.NET Core."*

