## 🎓 Stream Talking Points (Background Narrative)

Use these between coding steps to fill time naturally:

| Topic | What to say |
|---|---|
| **Why `Task.WhenAll`?** | "The bottleneck was disk I/O, not CPU. `Task.WhenAll` lets the OS schedule all 8 file reads concurrently. On a machine with an SSD and multiple cores, this is close to linear speedup." |
| **Why cache?** | "Arabic Islamic texts — the same queries get repeated constantly. `حضرت`, `مسجد`, `خلافت`. With a 30-minute sliding cache, repeat visitors get submillisecond responses." |
| **The double-highlight bug** | "This is a real correctness bug. The HTML was `<mark><mark>query</mark></mark>`. Browsers render it oddly and it breaks CSS selectors. The fix was separating concerns — one method extracts text, another method highlights it." |
| **`RegexOptions.Compiled`** | "This tells the .NET runtime to emit actual native machine code for the pattern. For a regex running on every search result, it's a measurable win." |
| **What's next (vectors)?** | "This refactor is the foundation for what comes next — semantic/vector search. Instead of `string.Contains`, we'll embed queries and passages as vectors and find results by cosine similarity. That's what the branch name hints at." |

