|---|---|---:|---:|---:|---:|---:|
| **v2 Parallel Task.WhenAll (after)** | حضرت | **927.5 µs** | 202.5 µs | **0.71** | 1 | 2.7 KB |
| v1 Sequential (before) | حضرت | 1,396.3 µs | 420.6 µs | 1.00 | 2 | 2.1 KB |
| **v2 Parallel Task.WhenAll (after)** | مسجد | **892.4 µs** | 94.9 µs | **0.99** | 1 | 2.7 KB |
| v1 Sequential (before) | مسجد | 929.0 µs | 176.7 µs | 1.03 | 1 | 2.1 KB |

**Point out on stream:**
- **Ratio column** — `0.71` = v2 is 29% faster on the hot path for `حضرت`
- **StdDev column** — v1 at 420µs vs v2 at 202µs = **v1 is twice as unpredictable**
- **Cold-start row** (warmup iteration, shown separately) = v1 28ms vs v2 22ms = **21% faster on first ever request**

**Say on stream:**
> *"StdDev is the hidden metric most people ignore. Low standard deviation means every user gets a consistent experience. High standard deviation means some users get 900µs and others get 1800µs — you can't predict it. v2 is not just faster on average, it's more reliable."*

